NFloattext.mcc/NFloattext.mcc

    NAME
        NFloattext.mcc -- Display wrapped text.

    SUPERCLASS
        NList.mcc

    DESCRIPTION
        Use NList wrapped entries to display paragraphs. This source defines
        version 19.74. By default the constructor supplies NList_Input FALSE
        and NList_TypeSelect_Char. An explicit TypeSelect takes precedence;
        Input TRUE also prevents this class from imposing character selection.
        NFloattext_Text borrows the source string. The legacy Floattext_Text
        alias copies it. Keep borrowed text valid and unchanged while the
        object uses it. Dispose the object through MUI. Copy and insertion
        failures do not consistently make construction fail.
        Set Align after construction and before supplying Text. The initial
        Align path accesses instance data before superclass construction and
        is subsequently overwritten by the local default; it is not a
        supported way to establish the requested alignment in this
        implementation.
        Align and Justify changes do not rebuild existing entries. Text
        replacement inserts with the stored alignment at that point, so tag
        order matters. Use independent replacement storage when prior text was
        copied by the class; the old allocation is freed before replacement.
        List_GetEntry is an alias of NFloattext_GetEntry. NList_GetEntry
        remains the superclass method and has different wrapped-entry
        semantics. Returned pointers are borrowed and may refer to either
        source storage or one reusable line buffer. Do not free them.
NFloattext.mcc/MUIA_NFloattext_Align

    NAME
        MUIA_NFloattext_Align -- Select alignment for subsequent text
        insertion.

    INPUTS
        Set/get; LONG. Header also declares initialization, but that
        constructor path is defective. Use ALIGN_LEFT (0), ALIGN_CENTER
        (0x0100), ALIGN_RIGHT (0x0200) or ALIGN_JUSTIFY (0x0400).

    FUNCTION
        Set stores value masked with 0x0700. Justify becomes TRUE only when
        the masked value equals ALIGN_JUSTIFY. Combined bits are not
        separately validated. Get returns the stored value.
        No existing entries are reinserted or reformatted by this setter. Set
        alignment before Text in a set message or in an earlier call. Initial
        effective alignment is left or justified according to the constructor
        Justify option; do not rely on an initial Align tag.
NFloattext.mcc/MUIA_NFloattext_Justify

    NAME
        MUIA_NFloattext_Justify -- Select justified or left alignment.

    INPUTS
        Initialize/set/get; BOOL, default FALSE. Floattext_Justify is an
        alias.

    FUNCTION
        Nonzero stores TRUE and ALIGN_JUSTIFY; zero stores FALSE and
        ALIGN_LEFT. A later Align tag can change both settings. During
        construction the NFloattext alias takes precedence over the legacy
        alias. During set, tags are processed in order. Existing entries are
        not rebuilt; this setting is used when Text is inserted.
NFloattext.mcc/MUIA_NFloattext_SkipChars

    NAME
        MUIA_NFloattext_SkipChars -- Supply characters for NList to skip.

    INPUTS
        Initialize/set/get; borrowed NUL-terminated char * or NULL. Backend
        default NULL.

    FUNCTION
        Translate to NList_SkipChars, including the legacy Floattext_SkipChars
        alias. NList stores the pointer without copying it and requests redraw
        on set. Keep the string readable while in use; get returns the
        borrowed pointer.
        Construction rewrites the first own tag, otherwise the first legacy
        tag. Set rewrites every matching tag in place. Get rewrites opg_AttrID
        before delegating. Message and tag storage must be writable. This
        class does not remove bytes from your source text.
NFloattext.mcc/MUIA_NFloattext_TabSize

    NAME
        MUIA_NFloattext_TabSize -- Set NList tab spacing.

    INPUTS
        Initialize/set/get; numeric size, backend default 8. Header type
        ULONG; backend stores LONG.

    FUNCTION
        Translate to NList_TabSize, including the legacy Floattext_TabSize
        alias. Backend set stores the value and requests redraw without local
        range validation. Use a positive representable size. Construction
        rewrites the first own tag or first legacy tag; set rewrites matching
        tags, and get rewrites opg_AttrID. Supply writable message/tag
        storage.
NFloattext.mcc/MUIA_NFloattext_Text

    NAME
        MUIA_NFloattext_Text -- Replace the displayed text.

    INPUTS
        Initialize/set/get; readable NUL-terminated STRPTR or NULL.

    FUNCTION
        Borrow this attribute value without copying. NULL clears the text.
        Wrapped display is provided by NList; keep source storage valid until
        replacement or disposal. Get returns the stored pointer without
        ownership transfer.
        Floattext_Text instead copies the input to owned storage. During
        construction the own attribute takes precedence. During set, each text
        tag clears entries and frees any old owned text before replacement;
        allocation failure can leave the object empty. Do not pass an alias
        into that old allocation as replacement input.
        Set Align or Justify before Text to insert with the requested
        alignment. The class ignores the InsertWrap result; an attribute set
        result is not proof of complete insertion.
NFloattext.mcc/MUIM_NFloattext_GetEntry

    NAME
        MUIM_NFloattext_GetEntry -- Read a displayed entry.

    SYNOPSIS
        DoMethod(obj, MUIM_NFloattext_GetEntry, pos, &entry);

    INPUTS
        pos -- Zero-based displayed entry index, or MUIV_NList_GetEntry_Active
        (-1). The backend also interprets -2 as logical line zero and -3 as
        the last inserted entry. entry -- Writable APTR storage.
        MUIM_List_GetEntry uses this same handler.

    FUNCTION
        Query entry information. A wrapped slice is normally copied into a
        reusable buffer and terminated with NUL. Copy its contents before
        another GetEntry call if it must survive. Unwrapped entries are
        returned directly from NList.
        If buffer allocation fails, return a pointer into the original text at
        the slice start. No terminator is added at the displayed line
        boundary, so the result is not guaranteed to contain only that line. A
        missing entry writes NULL.
        Do not free the returned pointer. Source replacement, list changes and
        disposal can invalidate source-backed results; a later call can
        overwrite or free the reusable buffer.

    RESULT
        Always TRUE, including missing entries and buffer allocation failure.
        Inspect the output pointer; TRUE does not prove a copied,
        line-terminated result.

